+import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.ts"
+
+export const noLiveSupervisorMatchesTheSupervisorPredicate = {
+  id: "01a07371-81f2-77cf-b789-528e4fdabbd0",
+  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
+  slug: "no-live-supervisor-matches-the-supervisor-predicate",
+  domainSlug: "workspace-package/seat-system",
+
+  claim:
+    "`isSupervisorCmdline` requires the literal `supervisor.ts` in a command line, and no file of that name is in the repository. It matches none of the live supervisors. The memory reaper draws the roots of its per-tree leg from that predicate, so the per-tree ceiling has no tree to measure and cannot fire. The unit test asserts the predicate against a command line shape the repository no longer produces, so a passing test reports on a predicate that can never match.",
+  evidence:
+    "Measured on the akasha checkout on 2026-09-05, by ryn, on a quiet tree.\n\nThe predicate is `SUPERVISOR_CMDLINE_RE = /^(?:\\S*\\/)?bun\\b.*supervisor\\.ts/` at `seat-system/seat-proc-liveness/seat-proc-liveness.module.code.ts:5`, read by `isSupervisorCmdline` at `:10`.\n\nRan that exact expression over `/proc`: 312 processes owned by uid 1000, 84 of them running bun, 0 matching. A live supervisor was among them and was not matched — pid 34855, `bun /var/home/walton/repos/akasha/seat-system/run-supervisor/run-supervisor.module.code.ts -a aawalton --agent-id 01a06c7b-...`.\n\nA zero and a blind instrument answer alike, so the expression was given a control in the same run: it still matches `bun tools/run-supervisor.ts` and `/usr/bin/bun /repo/seat-system/supervising/supervisor.ts`. The expression works. What it is looking for is gone. `git ls-files` names no file ending `supervisor.ts` anywhere in the tree; the entry point is `seat-system/run-supervisor/run-supervisor.module.code.ts`.\n\nThe sibling expression three lines below settles that this is staleness rather than intent. `SEAT_INFRA_CMDLINE_RE` at `:7` still names `packages/agents/oauth-proxy/src/main.ts`, and `git ls-files` tracks nothing at all under `packages/`; but that same expression carries an alternative spelled `messages-mcp(?:\\.module\\.code)?\\.ts`, which is the layout in use now. One expression was carried through the move and the one beside it was not.\n\nThe test is the part worth keeping. `seat-proc-liveness.module.test.ts:35` and `:40` assert `isSupervisorCmdline` holds of `bun supervisor.ts`, a command line nothing in this repository produces. The test passes. It proves the predicate can recognise a supervisor that no longer exists, which is a different claim from the one anybody reading a green run would take from it.\n\nWhat this reaches, established: `readSupervisorPids` at `seat-system/supervising/memory-reaper-read/memory-reaper-read.module.code.ts:28` collects tree roots by this predicate, and `memory-reaper-tick.module.code.ts:51` hands them to the per-tree leg. No roots, no per-tree kill. `MAX_TREE_PSS_GB` is dead configuration.\n\nWhat this reaches, NOT established and not to be repeated as though it were: `isAgentProcessCmdline` at `:18` is this predicate or the claude-child one, and `stop-seat`, `takeover-seat`, `seat-recovery`, `subagent-census`, `seat-proc-tree` and `subagent-sweep` all read from this module. Whether any of them judges a live seat dead was not tested.\n\nOne correction belonging in the record, because it is the same mistake this finding is about. Ryn's own working memory held that an earlier kill came from the per-tree ceiling at 32 GiB. That kill cannot have come from the per-tree leg. `MAX_RSS_GB` and `MAX_TREE_PSS_GB` are both 32, so the number 32 does not tell the two legs apart, and the leg was named from the number rather than from the evidence.",
+} as const satisfies Finding
